1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,413
Introduction to F S L Eyes.

2
00:00:02,413 --> 00:00:07,238
Load anatomical and functional NIfTI files and orient yourself in three planes.

3
00:00:07,238 --> 00:00:10,858
The goal is clear: Open files from the terminal.

4
00:00:11,708 --> 00:00:14,026
Visual inspection is an analysis step.

5
00:00:14,026 --> 00:00:18,663
F S L Eyes lets you examine image geometry and intensity directly.

6
00:00:18,663 --> 00:00:22,913
The orthographic view shows the same location in three anatomical planes.

7
00:00:22,913 --> 00:00:27,936
The overlay list controls which images are visible and how they are colored.

8
00:00:27,936 --> 00:00:35,277
Start by checking that the brain is oriented sensibly, the field of view is complete, and signal is present.

9
00:00:35,277 --> 00:00:39,527
For four-D images, move through volumes or open the time-series view.

10
00:00:39,527 --> 00:00:44,937
A file loading without an error does not prove that the data are usable.

11
00:00:45,787 --> 00:00:48,958
Now connect the idea to an observable check.

12
00:00:48,958 --> 00:00:52,921
First, launch F S L Eyes with a NIfTI path.

13
00:00:52,921 --> 00:00:55,695
Next, move the crosshair through the brain.

14
00:00:55,695 --> 00:00:58,866
Then, record one scanner coordinate and voxel coordinate.

15
00:00:58,866 --> 00:01:03,225
After that, for a bold file, open View then Time series.

16
00:01:03,225 --> 00:01:06,396
The command shown on screen is an example.

17
00:01:06,396 --> 00:01:12,341
Adapt its path to your own working directory and verify the target before running it.

18
00:01:13,191 --> 00:01:14,630
Quality Control Check.

19
00:01:14,630 --> 00:01:19,428
Confirm orientation, brain coverage, and visible signal before beginning preprocessing.

20
00:01:19,428 --> 00:01:24,225
A later pipeline cannot recover anatomy that was never acquired.

21
00:01:24,225 --> 00:01:31,902
A useful self-check is this: Why can the same point have both voxel and scanner coordinates?

22
00:01:31,902 --> 00:01:40,537
Voxel coordinates index the image grid; scanner/world coordinates locate that point in physical space using the image affine.

23
00:01:41,387 --> 00:01:45,968
To recap: First, inspect every key input and output visually.

24
00:01:45,968 --> 00:01:50,090
Next, use the overlay list and coordinate panel deliberately.

25
00:01:50,090 --> 00:01:56,503
Before continuing, make sure you can explain this objective: Open files from the terminal.
